Model facts
===========

src/open_omada_device_agent/contexts/device/omada_models_data.py lists TP-Link
Omada access point models with a few facts each: radio bands, spatial streams,
transmit power range, widest channel width, Wi-Fi generation and DFS support.
It is generated by scripts/gen_omada_models.py from the device model templates
of Omada Controller 6.3.0.111, reduced to those facts. No device identifiers,
firmware, feature lists or other template content are included. The table is
used only to pick which model an access point reports, for interoperability.
Where the table and TP-Link's published datasheet for a model disagree, the
datasheet is taken as correct.

The agent never downloads or installs TP-Link firmware.

Also credited, nothing taken: unifi-openwrt
(https://github.com/antoniocosta/unifi-openwrt) and unifi-emu
(https://github.com/jamesbraid/unifi-emu), whose reduced, credited model
catalogues for UniFi devices this table follows in approach.
